      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Excerpted, level-adjusted and faded for this video.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Replica makes it easier for designers, product managers, and engineers to explore ideas together, get feedback earlier, and iterate without starting from scratch.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Unlike generic AI prototyping tools, Replica uses your team&rsquo;s existing components, patterns, and documentation to guide what gets created.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Collaborate and gather feedback: Publish prototypes to an optional, self-hosted Replica Hub where teammates can explore them and leave comments.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Adapt Replica to your team: Customize the open-source tooling and guidance to fit your product and workflows.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Replica helps teams move from conversations to tangible experiences faster, so they can test assumptions, explore possibilities, and make better-informed product decisions together.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Replica is available now as an open-source project under the MIT license.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:02.845Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can start prototyping locally or set up Replica Hub to share prototypes with your team.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
